@aryanmaurya1 Fixed path of the assets directory.

The previous rule ignores **directories** under the assets directory but it fails in ignoring **files** that are inside the assets directory. Though I don't have a proper explanation to prove why behind it but still I did a small experiment that proves the statement.

<img width="1280" alt="Screenshot 2021-09-04 at 8 39 37 AM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/46771418/132080818-e8983177-74a9-4bbc-92c4-fa22d8b0d0fc.png">

Fixes #173.

- The expected block time is set to 1 sec;
- The call of `process_queue` is placed in the `on_idle` hook which is executed after all normal extrinsics (those with `DispatchClass::Normal`) have been processed, as opposed to having it as an inherent extrinsic which would have to be run before normal dispatchables;
- The normal extrinsics max weight is set to 25% of the total block weight which guarantees the `on_idle` hook will be executed in every block.

**Release notes:**
Replacing the procedure of handling message queue to something similar to what will be used in production mode. Messages are handled immediately -- i.e. in the same block they are submitted in the message queue (if block gas limit is sufficient). Block time is also reduced to 1 second. Latency of the network theoretically goes down (better) by 18x factor.

Given the following code:

```php
final class OtherClassConstruct
{
    public function run()
    {
        return [OtherClass3::class, '__construct'];
    }
}
```

It currently produce:

```diff
+        return function ($property) : void {
+            (new \Rector\Tests\CodeQuality\Rector\Array_\CallableThisArrayToAnonymousFunctionRector\Source\OtherClass3())->__construct($property);
+        };
```

which make a double call `__construct`, first on `new`, then call `->__construct()`. It should be skipped.
